The psl crate compiles in Mozilla's Public Suffix List
(https://publicsuffix.org/list/public_suffix_list.dat), which the crate keeps
as data/rules.txt and src/list.rs. The crate's own code is under the MIT
license or the Apache License 2.0, but the list carries this notice:

  This Source Code Form is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public
  License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL was not distributed with this
  file, You can obtain one at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.

The text of the Mozilla Public License 2.0 is in the file MPL-2.0 next to
this one. The crate as published on crates.io, list included, is in
/usr/local/share/randomcontainers/yara-x/crate-sources/ in this image.
